            <ArticleTitle>Primary dysmenorrhoea--evidence for complementary medicine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>869</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary dysmenorrhoea is the occurrence of painful menstrual cramps in the absence of pelvic pathology. This review discusses alternative approaches to the management of this debilitating condition.</AbstractText>
